course: dictionary
lesson: 8969
title: Singers and their voices
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A singer is a person who sings. A singer can be someone who sings as a job, or just very well. A singer can also be one person in a choir, singing at that moment. Context helps you see which meaning fits. «The Queen asks for the list of the singers in the last concert» means people who sing at a concert.
explain: Sometimes a sentence tells you a lot about the singer. «A song made with a cloned voice of a famous singer went viral and was then removed.» A famous singer is a person many people know, and their voice can be copied. Viral means many people shared it quickly, and removed means it was taken away.
explain: Singers also use special sounds. «Vibrato is a controlled wobble in the voice that singers use on purpose.» Because the word says on purpose, you know it is a choice, not an accident. A nervous shake is different, because a singer does not plan it.
fact: A singer is a person who sings.
fact: A singer can be a job, such as an opera singer or a pop singer.
fact: A singer can also be one person in a choir, singing at this moment.
fact: «Vibrato» is a controlled wobble in the voice that singers use on purpose.
fact: A lead singer is the main singer in a band or group.
exercise: «The Queen asks for the list of the singers in the last concert.» Who are the singers? | Tickets sold at the door | Instruments played in a band | *People who sing | Seats in the hall
exercise: «Vibrato is a controlled wobble in the voice that singers use on purpose.» What is vibrato? | *A controlled wobble in the voice, used on purpose | A loud drum sound | A kind of dance | A nervous shake
exercise: A choir has 12 singers. 5 singers go home early. How many singers are left? | 5 | 17 | 12 | *7
test: In «a singer, singers», what kind of word is singer? | Verb | Adjective | *Noun | Adverb
test: «The choir singer hit the high note.» Who hit the high note? | *A person who sings in a choir | A piano | The concert hall | The note
exam: Which word names a voice trick that singers use on purpose, not a nervous shake? | *Vibrato | A cough | Stage fright | Hiccups
